{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nWe have reached Weimar, and the air here is thick with the scent of damp earth and history. I am lodging near Goethe, who receives me with the warmth I have long hoped for. This evening, the Grand Duke joined us for tea. I sat beside him on the sofa, and we conversed until nearly ten. It is a profound pleasure to speak with men of such stature, yet I confess my mind is already turning back to our quiet rooms in Berlin.\n\nTomorrow, Zelter and I shall ride in Goethe’s carriage to the Grand Duke’s botanical garden at Belvedere. I imagine the plants will be more orderly than the human soul, which is a comfort. The journey has been tiring, but the company, stimulating. I hope the house is comfortable in my absence. Kiss the boys for me, especially little Ludwig, who misses his father’s sharp tongue.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219170,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":196,"prompt_tokens":957,"total_tokens":1153,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-msUX90XtaokkcRwuNlrLKhe6XNPDJw3l","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":957,"prompt_ms":909.309,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.950166144200627,"prompt_per_second":1052.44751784047,"predicted_n":196,"predicted_ms":4587.183,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.524015384615385,"predicted_per_second":42.509749447536755}}